* Function closures

⟪GTI18N_570e535e_000001⟫ functions may be closures. A closure is a function value that references variables from outside its body. The function may access and assign to the referenced variables; in this sense the function is "bound" to the variables.

For example, the ⟪GTI18N_570e535e_000002⟫adder⟪GTI18N_570e535e_000003⟫ function returns a closure. Each closure is bound to its own ⟪GTI18N_570e535e_000004⟫sum⟪GTI18N_570e535e_000005⟫ variable.

